+<details><summary>What the real frame does beyond this toy</summary>
+<ul>
+ <li><b>The flow frame first.</b> The bus step turns the board a whole number of quarter turns so the source-to-destination direction points along +x (<code>flow_frame.py</code>: exact on the 0.1 mm lattice, and turned back after). A board whose differential pairs have the other chirality is also turned over in memory. So the trunk always runs west to east, and the destination's <i>west</i> face is the one facing the source.</li>
+ <li><b>The trunk</b> is one straight line from the source's pad box centre through the destination's. The faces are the pad boxes' own, grown to where the stubs end.</li>
+ <li><b>The rings</b> go round the destination's <b>hull</b>: its pads, the berths, and other parts' pads within a lane's reach of them. Their lanes stack outward in berth order, the lane that berths first innermost. A part standing in that stack is passed on the inside when the ring's lanes fit between it and the destination, and gone round when they do not. Each ring starts outside the destination's corner, stepped back along the trunk until it clears the hull (<code>Hk</code>).</li>
