 <h2 id="cpsat">1 &nbsp; CP-SAT: the discrete plan (<code>whole_solve.py</code>)</h2>
-<p>Bus lanes leave the source BGA in one order (the <b>launch order</b>, set by each lane's <i>tooth</i>) and must arrive at the destination in another (the <b>berth order</b>). Every pair that is inverted between the two <b>has to cross</b>. Two copper lanes cannot cross on the same layer, so at each crossing one lane is on <span class="F">F.Cu</span> and the other on <span class="B">B.Cu</span>. Each layer change costs a <b>via</b>. Each lane also starts on a fixed layer (its tooth) and ends on a fixed layer (its berth).</p>
-<p>The CP-SAT model is exactly that puzzle: booleans for "which lane is on top at this crossing", integers for "where along the trunk the crossing happens", and constraints tying them together. It <b>minimises vias and proves the minimum</b>. Below, an instance of that puzzle with the numbers shrunk to 5 lanes.</p>
+<p>Bus lanes leave the source BGA in one order (the <b>launch order</b>: the teeth, unrolled) and must arrive at the destination in another (the <b>berth order</b>: the destination unrolled from the cut, <a href="#frame">0c</a>). Every pair that is inverted between the two <b>has to cross</b>, once, at a position in <code>u</code> both lanes share. Two copper lanes cannot cross on the same layer, so at each crossing they are on different layers: on two layers one is on <span class="F">F.Cu</span> and the other on <span class="B">B.Cu</span>. Each layer change costs a <b>via</b>. A lane whose stub ends on the surface starts (or ends) on that layer; a lane whose stub ends in a via may leave it on any layer its run fits on.</p>
+<p>The CP-SAT model is exactly that puzzle, for every lane at once: booleans for "which lane is on which layer at this crossing", integers for "where along <code>u</code> the crossing happens" and "where each lane changes layer" (up to three changes a lane), and constraints tying them together. It <b>minimises vias and proves the minimum</b>. Below, an instance of that puzzle with the numbers shrunk to 5 lanes on two layers.</p>
 
