 <h3>1b &nbsp; Where along the trunk: time-window constraints</h3>
-<p>Booleans decide <i>who</i> crosses. Integers decide <i>where</i>. Each crossing gets an integer position <code>t</code> along the trunk, limited to a window (the stretch where both lanes exist and have finished their earlier crossings). Crossings that compete for the same lanes must be at least a lane pitch apart. That is the <code>AddNoOverlap</code> constraint on optional intervals in <code>whole_solve.py</code>.</p>
+<p>Booleans decide <i>who</i> crosses. Integers decide <i>where</i>. Each crossing gets an integer position <code>t</code> in <code>u</code> (on a grid of a fifth of a lane pitch), limited to a window: the stretch where both lanes exist, clear of a pair's end connector, and for two lanes on the same ring short of the earlier one's berth. A lane's crossings along it must be at least a lane pitch apart (less for a lane sweeping steeply across the others). That is the <code>AddNoOverlap</code> constraint on optional intervals in <code>whole_solve.py</code>. Layer changes are positions in <code>u</code> too, with rooms of their own:</p>
+<ul>
+ <li>a change keeps a via's room from its own lane's crossings, and a single lane's change keeps a change's room from both its ends (a pair's, its <b>dive room</b>);</li>
+ <li>no change in a band along the source's facing side, where the teeth stand and the lanes have not spread yet;</li>
+ <li>a lane leaving the surface may change layer right at its stub's end only where a via there is measured clear of every other net's copper on every layer;</li>
+ <li>two neighbouring lanes' changes are staggered along <code>u</code>, so their vias clear the via-to-via rule;</li>
+ <li>no change where the lane's reference passes within a via's reach of another part's pad (the <b>built-in via cuts</b>, on the rings too).</li>
